# r1115 phase 11 (runner-11), boot 2 of the p11a world (after pth_a2.qb and save-all): SQ-PTH-16 (value 6 migrated),
# SQ-PTH-07 (items held across a restart), SQ-PTH-14d (the demoted arrow of SQ-PTH-14c keeps its demotion).
# srv toml before this boot: a [leaf_piles] table with slowFromLayers = 6 put back at the top of
# config/creativecompat-common.toml (the live file's shape before the migration).
pace 1

## SQ-PTH-16 | boot 2: [leaf_piles] slowFromLayers 6 moved to [surface.passthrough.leaf_pile] minLayers 6
bootexpect Done \(
bootexpect \[leaf_piles\] slowFromLayers \(6\) moved to \[surface\.passthrough\.leaf_pile\] minLayers \(6\)
bootreject LeafPileSlowMixin
bootreject Mixin apply failed
shell grep -c '^\[leaf_piles\]' config/creativecompat-common.toml || true; awk '/\[surface\.passthrough\.leaf_pile\]/{f=1} f&&/minLayers/{print; exit}' config/creativecompat-common.toml; grep -n 'moved to' logs/latest.log | cut -c1-260

## SQ-PTH-14d | after the restart: the demoted arrow (x 1156) vanishes at its first minute, the other three stay
> pbot spawn P 1150.5 -60 990.5 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 5
> execute as @e[type=minecraft:arrow,x=1150,y=-62,z=995,dx=16,dy=6,dz=10] run data get entity @s life
> execute as @e[type=minecraft:arrow,x=1150,y=-62,z=995,dx=16,dy=6,dz=10] run data get entity @s Pos
> zpth watch a14c 700 100
waitlog watch done a14c 60
> execute as @e[type=minecraft:arrow,x=1150,y=-62,z=995,dx=16,dy=6,dz=10] run data get entity @s Pos
look the x 1156.5 arrow gone (gone line) once its life passes 1200; 1158, 1160, 1162 stay

## SQ-PTH-07 | items of SQ-PTH-06 still held after the restart, CreativeCompatPass in their data; web removed: they fall, NoGravity back to 0b
> zpth mod i06
> data get entity @e[tag=i06fast,limit=1]
> setblock 1000 -57 1120 minecraft:air
sleep 3
> zpth mod i06
look before: same positions as SQ-PTH-06, ng=true, data has a CreativeCompatPass key; after: y -60 (ground), ng=false

## SQ-PTH-12b | the item dropped when the web holding the second pickarang was broken (pth_a2 SQ-PTH-12)
> execute as @e[type=minecraft:item,x=1106,y=-62,z=999,dx=5,dy=5,dz=5] run data get entity @s Item
look one item is quark:pickarang

## SQ-PTH-10b | explosive arrow from the far side (bot turned by tp; zpth face was broken in pth_a2), then both cells holding the hanging no-pickup arrow broken
> fill 1080 -60 1000 1082 -58 1002 minecraft:cobweb
> zpth watchnew nock_enough_arrows:explosive_arrow e10b 400 2 1081.5 -59 1001.5 7
> clear P
> tp P 1081.5 -60 1007.5 180 0
> item replace entity P weapon.mainhand with minecraft:bow
> give P nock_enough_arrows:explosive_arrow 1
> zpth use P
> zpth release P 20
sleep 4
> zpth mod e10b
> execute if block 1081 -59 1001 minecraft:cobweb run say PTH10b-centre-intact
> execute if block 1081 -59 1002 minecraft:cobweb run say PTH10b-edge-intact
> zpth near minecraft:arrow 1081.5 -58.5 1001.5 2
> zpth watchnew minecraft:arrow a10b 100 2 1081.5 -58.5 1001 1
> setblock 1081 -59 1001 minecraft:air destroy
> setblock 1081 -59 1000 minecraft:air destroy
sleep 4
> zpth near minecraft:arrow 1081.5 -59 1001 3
expect PTH10b-centre-intact$
look e10b stops in the cube with no blast (webs intact); the no-pickup arrow falls once both cells are gone

